+## Integration scope
+
+This is a focused external-contributor review technique, not a complete CI audit.
+Project controls and pinning policy take precedence over the heuristics below.
+Trace actual downstream action/shell sinks, effective token permissions, runner
+isolation, reusable callers, caches and artifacts before deciding a path is safe.
+Values passed through `with:` or `env:` can reach an unsafe action or shell sink.
+A `pull_request` event, first-party tag, or trigger name alone proves no safety.
+Do not execute illustrative payloads, probe GitHub, publish findings, or change
+workflow permissions without the corresponding user authorization.
+
